It looks like the events REST storage initialization is using the core events registry, which uses the core events strategy. The events strategy (at `pkg/registry/events/event/strategy.go`) is unreferenced and unused.

I was able to get the `regarding...` and `reportingController` field selectors to work by doing the following:
1. removing `pkg/registry/events/event/...`
2. add `reportingController` to the field set generated by `pkg/registry/core/event/strategy.go#ToSelectableFields`
3. adjust the `AddFieldLabelConversionsForEvent` in `pkg/apis/events/{v1,v1beta1}/conversion.go` to map from events.k8s.io field selector names to the fieldset names constructed in `pkg/registry/core/event/strategy.go#ToSelectableFields`:

```go
func AddFieldLabelConversionsForEvent(scheme *runtime.Scheme) error {
	mapping := map[string]string{
		"reason":                    "reason",
		"regarding.kind":            "involvedObject.kind",
		"regarding.namespace":       "involvedObject.namespace",
		"regarding.name":            "involvedObject.name",
		"regarding.uid":             "involvedObject.uid",
		"regarding.apiVersion":      "involvedObject.apiVersion",
		"regarding.resourceVersion": "involvedObject.resourceVersion",
		"regarding.fieldPath":       "involvedObject.fieldPath",
		"reportingController":       "reportingController",
		"type":                      "type",
		"metadata.namespace":        "metadata.namespace",
		"metadata.name":             "metadata.name",
	}
	return scheme.AddFieldLabelConversionFunc(SchemeGroupVersion.WithKind("Event"),
		func(label, value string) (string, string, error) {
			mappedLabel, ok := mapping[label]
			if !ok {
				return "", "", fmt.Errorf("field label not supported: %s", label)
			}
			return mappedLabel, value, nil
		},
	)
}
```
